Package: taos-gpu
Version: 0.1.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: jaylfc <jaylfc25@gmail.com>
Priority: optional
Section: admin
Depends: udev
Description: taOS display GPU policy: NVIDIA cards are compute only by default
 Provides the taos-gpu command. It reads sysfs, picks the GPU that drives the
 display (an integrated GPU by default, never a discrete NVIDIA card while an
 integrated GPU exists), and generates a udev rule exposing it as
 /dev/dri/taos-display, a compositor session environment file and a modprobe
 config that keeps nouveau and nvidia-drm off the display. The display GPU can
 be chosen at install time and switched later with taos-gpu set-display.
